# Tutorial 06 — slabs, flat and shed roofs, the canopy and the stair to the upper floor.
title: Floors, roofs and stairs
summary: Slabs, flat and shed roofs with overhangs, a stair between levels and the canopy
---
speed 18
open new
runfile setup/cedar-walls.scr
runfile setup/cedar-openings.scr
zoom window -2500,-2500 23500,12000
caption "Floor slabs" "SLAB from points: 250 mm oak floors"
type SLAB Thickness 250 Offset 0 -150,1350 6150,1350 6150,10150 -150,10150 C
type SLAB 5850,-150 11150,-150 11150,7650 5850,7650 C
type SLAB 11000,3050 21150,3050 21150,10150 11000,10150 C
wait 1
caption "The porch" "Offset raises a slab above its level: 180 mm"
type SLAB Thickness 200 Offset 180 11600,0 17600,0 17600,3200 11600,3200 C
wait 1
caption "Flat roof" "Kind, Overhang and Base (eave height) are options"
type ROOF Kind Flat Overhang 700 Base 6200 Thickness 320 0,1500 6000,1500 6000,10000 0,10000 C
wait 1
caption "Shed roof" "A 4° mono-pitch plate with a deep 1.3 m overhang on the tower"
type ROOF Kind Shed Pitch 4 Overhang 1300 Base 7200 Thickness 300 6000,0 11000,0 11000,7500 6000,7500 C
type ROOF Kind Flat Overhang 350 Base 6400 11200,5600 16200,5600 16200,10000 11200,10000 C
wait 1
caption "The canopy" "A 450 mm slab at 3.75 m over the whole entry wing"
type SLAB Thickness 450 Offset 3750 11000,-400 21600,-400 21600,10300 11000,10300 C
wait 1
caption "Stair" "STAIR runs to the Upper Floor level; the risers are computed"
type STAIR Width 1100 Top "Upper Floor" 10200,1300 90
wait 1.5
caption "The upper floor" "Set the level current and draw its slab"
type LEVEL Set "Upper Floor"
type SLAB Thickness 250 Offset 0 0,1500 11000,1500 11000,10000 0,10000 C
type LEVEL Set "Ground Floor"
caption "In 3D" "Floors, roofs, canopy and stair"
click mode 3D
wait 1
type SEISO
wait 1
orbit 70 4
click mode 2D
caption "Next: rooms and annotation" "Tutorial 07 documents the plan"
wait 3
